# Model weights and the llama.cpp runtime binary are NEVER committed. They are fetched by
# tools/fetch_models.py from URLs pinned to an immutable upstream revision and verified
# against the sha256 digests in pack/models.lock.toml.
#
# Committing them would put ~1.6 GiB of binaries with their own licences into every clone
# of the base repository — the exact thing on-demand Capability Packs exist to avoid.
*
!.gitignore
